  "description": "Dear Team,\n\nBelow is the current Docker Compose configuration for our two core containers. The **web** service runs the latest\u202fNGINX image under the container name **my_web**. It exposes ports\u202f80\u202f\u2192\u202f80 and\u202f443\u202f\u2192\u202f443, and is attached to the **frontend** network. Environment variables set for this service are\u202fENV=production,\u202fDEBUG=false, and\u202fMAX_CONNECTIONS=100. Its document root is mounted read\u2011only from **/var/www** on the host to **/usr/share/nginx/html** inside the container. The container will always restart (restart policy\u202f*always*), carries the label **com.example.description=Web server**, and resolves the hostname **db** to **10.0.0.2** via an extra host entry. Logging is handled by the\u202fjson\u2011file\u202fdriver with a maximum size of\u202f10\u202fMiB per file and up to\u202f3\u202ffiles retained. Resource limits are set to a CPU share of\u202f512 and a memory cap of\u202f256\u202fMiB.\n\nThe **db** service uses the\u202fpostgres:13\u202fimage and is named **my_db**. It receives two environment variables\u2014**POSTGRES_PASSWORD=secret** and **POSTGRES_DB=mydb**\u2014and maps the host port\u202f5432\u202fdirectly to the container. Persistent storage is provided by binding **/var/lib/postgresql/data** on the host to the same path inside the container. This service restarts unless stopped (restart policy\u202f*unless\u2011stopped*) and is labeled **tier=backend**. Memory is limited to\u202f512\u202fMiB with a swap ceiling of\u202f1\u202fGiB. Additional capabilities include adding **NET_ADMIN** and dropping **MKNOD**. Finally, the startup command overrides the default with\u202f`postgres -c max_connections=200`."
